cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the journal article below."
title: "R-Clustering"
abstract: >-
  R-Clustering is a time series clustering method that applies convolutional
  architectures with randomly selected kernel parameters. Features are extracted
  by convolving the input series with random kernels and computing the
  proportion of positive values (PPV), followed by dimensionality reduction and
  clustering. The method is evaluated on the UCR archive and compared against
  reference clustering algorithms in terms of accuracy, computational efficiency
  and scalability.
